+
+**Comm-complexity result.** Confirmed its decisive computation:
+comparison matrix `M[pi,q]=[pi(i)<pi(j)]` has exactly `n!` distinct rows and
+GF(2) rank `binom(n,2)` for `n=2..7` → ranks `1,3,6,10,15,21`. Since the matrix
+has only `binom(n,2)` columns, `rank <= binom(n,2)` holds for every field, so
+`log2 rank = O(log n)`, strictly weaker than `log2(n!) = Theta(n log n)`.
+Its logic is sound: `D(G_n)=S(n)` is definitional; `n!` leaves force
+`D >= log2(n!)`; Sergeev's `S(n)=log2(n!)+o(n)` caps every CC lower bound on
+`G_n` at the classical `Theta(n log n)`. The no-bridge arguments (unbounded
+local computation; `1^n` admits only the monotone Ferrers split; KW-depth and
+OBDD-width bridges need a split of the function's own input, absent for the
+scalar `S(n)`) are correct, and the inference "`Omega(n log n)` comparisons to
+sort ⇒ `Omega(n log n)` space to compute `S(n)`" is invalid because a machine
+computing the scalar need not represent a sorting strategy.
+Not independently re-audited: the 64-page board novelty scan (agent-reported).
+
+**Spectral result.** Confirmed its decisive arithmetic: `p(n)=2^{Theta(sqrt n)}`
+(`log2 p(n)/sqrt n ≈ 2.75, 2.96, 3.13` at `n=100,200,400`) and
+`log2 p(n) << 0.25·n·log2(n)^2` (e.g. `41.85` vs `2921` at `n=200`, `44.74` vs
+`3413` at `n=224`) — so RSK-shape/rank-generated invariants cannot reach the
+`2^{(1/4-o(1)) n log2^2 n}` barrier. Its lemmas are sound: L1 (`min(|R_t|,|V|)`
+range bound) is trivial; L2 uses the classical fact that the adjacent-transposition
+operator has at most `p(n)` distinct eigenvalues; L3 observes that rank-generating
+functions aggregate across depths while depth `t` and relation-count `r` diverge,
+and Möbius is a single isomorphism-invariant integer per state — both posteriori,
+not independent certificates. Sergeev's `o(n)` excess rules out an additive
+`Omega(n)` spectral-gap lower bound. No bridge back to uniform `S(n)`.
+Not independently re-derived: the classical spectrum theorem (literature) and
+the ledger/board novelty audit (agent-reported). Its own caveat that only the
+*named* invariants are novel, not the broader algebraic route
+(`algebraic-invariants-sortbound-20261101` etc.), is accepted.
